# Line endings, made deterministic for every clone regardless of the
# cloner's core.autocrlf, in Alonzo's shape. The repository stores LF; the
# working copy gets what each consumer needs:
#   - Rust, its manifests, the toolchain file and the page's files are LF on
#     every platform, as rustfmt writes them.
#   - A cartridge, a source, a library and a content sheet are VLA (.vla)
#     and get CRLF on checkout, as Alonzo's cartridges and Frazaro's corpus
#     files do, so that the language's reference implementation, whose line
#     reader treats a bare LF as text, can read them too.
#   - A built .wasm is bytes.
# Everything else is ordinary text (LF in the repo, the platform's default
# on checkout) or binary.
* text=auto
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.vla text eol=crlf
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.vla linguist-language=Lisp